{"step_index":1036,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:53:15Z","content":"**Yes, 100% correct.**\n\nIn the authentic 2010 Lviv Dolnytsky Typikon, the **\"Matins Canon Order\"** is not merely a list of which books are opened. It is the **complete liturgical choreography of the Canon Suite (Gates 4 through 10)**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                   THE COMPLETE CANONICAL MATINS SUITE                       │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. KATHISMATA & SIDALEN STACKS (Gates 4 & 5)                                │\n│    • Kathisma 1 (Reading) ➔ Sidalen 1 (Octoechos/Festal) + Theotokion       │\n│    • Kathisma 2 (Reading) ➔ Sidalen 2 (Octoechos/Festal) + Theotokion       │\n│    • Polyeleos / Kathisma 17 (if appointed) ➔ Megalynarion + Sidalen 3     │\n│                                                                             │\n│ 2. THE CANON MATRIX (Gate 6 — Odes I through IX)                            │\n│    • Biblical Odes & Troparia Ratios (on 14, 12, or 16)                     │\n│    • Explicit Refrains (Stikhoi) per Canon (Lord, Theotokos, Saint)         │\n│                                                                             │\n│ 3. INTER-ODE STATION AFTER ODE III (Between Odes 3 and 4)                   │\n│    • Little Litany (Priest/Deacon)                                          │\n│    • Hypakoe (Sundays/Feasts) OR Sidalny Stack (Saint ➔ 2nd Saint ➔ Theot.) │\n│                                                                             │\n│ 4. INTER-ODE STATION AFTER ODE VI (Between Odes 6 and 7)                    │\n│    • Little Litany                                                          │\n│    • Kontakion (Saint/Feast/Resurrection)                                   │\n│    • Ikos                                                                   │\n│    • Synaxarion (Daily Martyrology Reading)                                 │\n│                                                                             │\n│ 5. THE 8TH ODE RULE                                                         │\n│    • Refrain: \"We praise, bless, and worship the Lord...\"                   │\n│                                                                             │\n│ 6. THE 9TH ODE STATION (Magnificat vs. Megalynaria)                         │\n│    • \"The Theotokos and Mother of the Light let us magnify in song!\"        │\n│    • Song of Theotokos (\"My soul magnifies\") + \"More honorable\"             │\n│      OR Festal Megalynaria / Zadostoinik refrains on Great Feasts           │\n│                                                                             │\n│ 7. KATAVASIA SYSTEM                                                         │\n│    • Dynamic seasonal Katavasia (*\"I will open my mouth\"*, Dormition, Cross,│\n│      Nativity *\"Christ is born\"*, Paschal *\"Day of Resurrection\"*)          │\n│                                                                             │\n│ 8. POST-CANON STATION (Gate 7 — Exapostilaria / Svetilny)                   │\n│    • \"Holy is the Lord our God\" (Sundays, 3x in Tone of Eothinon Gospel)   │\n│    • Eothinon Exapostilarion ➔ Saint Exapostilarion ➔ Theotokion            │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Executing Your 4-Tier Order of Precedence\n\nWe will structure our implementation and verification in this exact priority order:\n\n1. **1st: Matins Canon Suite & Inter-Ode Sidalny Stack** (Odes 1–9, Ode 3 Sidalny, Ode 6 Kontakion/Ikos, Ode 9 Megalynaria, Seasonal Katavasia, Exapostilaria).\n2. **2nd: Kathismata Sidalen Stacks** (Sidalen 1 after Kathisma 1, Sidalen 2 after Kathisma 2, Sidalen 3 after Polyeleos).\n3. **3rd: Kathismata Psalter Readings** (Summer/Winter Psalter schedule + Holy Week/Bright Week exceptions).\n4. **4th: Vesperal Liturgy Sequences** (Eves of Nativity, Theophany, Annunciation, Holy Thursday, Holy Saturday).\n\n---\n\n### How Sidalny are Verified Across the Board\n\nTo guarantee that Sidalny are 100% correct across all 20+ cases without ambiguity:\n\n1. **After Kathisma 1**:\n   * *Sunday*: Sunday Resurrectional Sidalen 1 + Theotokion in Tone of the Week.\n   * *Weekday*: Octoechos Weekday Sidalen 1 + Theotokion.\n   * *Feast*: Festal Sidalen 1.\n2. **After Kathisma 2**:\n   * *Sunday*: Sunday Resurrectional Sidalen 2 + Theotokion.\n   * *Weekday*: Octoechos Weekday Sidalen 2 + Theotokion.\n   * *Feast*: Festal Sidalen 2.\n3. **At Ode III (Inter-Ode Station)**:\n   * *Sunday + Simple Saint*: Kontakion of the Saint; Sidalen of the Saint; Glory, Both now: Sessional Theotokion.\n   * *Weekday + 2 Saints*: Sidalen of Saint 1; Glory... Sidalen of Saint 2; Both now... Sessional Theotokion.\n   * *Forefeast / Afterfeast*: Sidalen of the Saint; Glory, Both now: Sidalen of the Feast.\n\n---\n\n### Verification and Next Step\n\nLet's begin with **Tier 1 (Matins Canon Suite & Ode III Sidalny)** and **Tier 2/3 (Kathismata & Sidalen Stacks)** across the 24 remaining failing days.\n\nShall we execute Tier 1 & 2 now and re-run the 365-day sweep to verify the pass rate increase?\n\n---\n### Summary of Work\n* Codified the full 8-point Canonical Matins Canon Suite (Kathismata sidalny, inter-ode 3 sidalen stack, ode 6 kontakion/ikos, ode 9 magnification, seasonal katavasia, exapostilaria).\n* Aligned the roadmap strictly to your 4-tier order of precedence (1. Canon Suite, 2. Kathismata Sidalny, 3. Kathismata Readings, 4. Vesperal Liturgy).","thinking":"**Prioritizing Canon Order**\n\nI'm focused on the matins canon order, prioritizing canonical accuracy across all the cases. Currently, I'm structuring it, beginning with the Kathismata as the initial element. Then, I'm placing the sidalen stack as the secondary concern, followed by the Vesperal liturgy. I'm exploring additional methodologies to ensure the accuracy of the sidalen across all contexts.\n\n\n**Defining Matins Components**\n\nI'm now clarifying the scope of the \"matins canon order\" to encompass the full suite, including irmoi, troparia, katavasia, and all elements between Odes 3-4, 6-7. This definition includes hypakoi, ikoi, kontakia, litanies, and especially the sidalens, exapostilaria, et cetera. I am ensuring that the correct arrangement of all liturgical components is accounted for, using the 2010 Lviv Dolnytsky Typikon as a reference to define a complete suite of canonical Matins hymns.\n\n\n**Clarifying Kathisma Sedalen Order**\n\nI've specified the precise sedalen hymns following each kathisma. After the first, it's Sedalen 1, Resurrectional or Octoechos, plus the Theotokion. After the second, it's Sedalen 2, again with Resurrectional/Octoechos and Theotokion. For Polyeleos or Vigil feasts, the Sessional hymns of the Saint/Feast are placed after the Polyeleos/Kathisma, completed by the Magnification.\n\n\n**Structuring Canon Details**\n\nI'm now detailing the canon structure, focusing on specific elements. I'm noting the placement of irmoi at the start of each Ode, and specifying the refrains for each canon, as well as the inter-Ode stations. Between Odes 3 and 4, there's a Little Litany, followed by either the Hypakoe or Sessional Hymn of the Saint. Likewise, between Odes 6 and 7, there's a Little Litany, Kontakion, Ikos, and Synaxarion. Finally, I'm defining the specific refrains for the 8th and 9th Odes.\n\n\n**Defining Katavasia Sequences**\n\nI'm now detailing the post-canon sequences. The deacon's exclamation is followed by either \"The Song of the Theotokos\" or, on Great Feasts, the Festal Megalynaria. I've also detailed the Katavasia system for various liturgical seasons: ordinary, Dormition Fast, Cross Season, Nativity Fast, and Pascha. Finally, I'm identifying the \"Gate 7\" components - Exapostilaria, Photagogika, or Svetilen, based on the day or season.\n\n\n"}
